<article class="env-corollary" id="06B0">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06B0">Corollary <span data-tag="06B0">7.3.8.6</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a simplicial set and let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories. Then the collection of $U$-colimit diagrams $K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is closed under levelwise $U$-colimits in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{Fun}(K^{\triangleright }, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ (see Definition <a data-tag="06A7" href="/tag/06A7">7.1.8.13</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $L$ be a simplicial set and let $f: L^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}( K^{\triangleright }, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ be a diagram, which we identify with a map $F: K^{\triangleright } \times L^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. Then $f$ is a levelwise $U$-colimit diagram (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="06A7" href="/tag/06A7">7.1.8.13</a>) if and only if $F$ satisfies conditions $(a)$ and $(3)$ of Variant <a data-tag="06AZ" href="/tag/06AZ">7.3.8.5</a>. If $f$ carries vertex $\ell \in L$ to an $F$-colimit diagram in $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, then $F$ also satisfies condition $(b)$ of Variant <a data-tag="06AZ" href="/tag/06AZ">7.3.8.5</a>. It follows that $F$ also satisfies condition $(1)$: that is, $f$ carries the cone point of $L^{\triangleright }$ to an $F$-colimit diagram. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
